 ◆ self-host                                                                                                      v1.0.0

  Home network

  ╭───────────────╮      ╭────────╮      ╭───────────────╮
  │ phones        │──────│ router │──────│ this computer │
  │ TVs · laptops │      ╰───┬────╯      │ 192.168.1.20  │
  ╰───────────────╯      internet ✗      ╰───────────────╯

  Phones, TVs and laptops on the same Wi-Fi or router as this computer can open your Apps at
  192.168.1.20. Nobody on the internet can.

  What is a LAN address?
  The address of this computer on your home or office network, like 192.168.1.20. Your router
  usually hands it out. Other devices type it into a browser, followed by an App's port. self-host
  finds it on this machine and uses it only to build App links; change it if this computer has
  more than one.

  The internet
  Nobody on the internet can open your Apps unless your router forwards ports to this computer.
  self-host never sets that up.

  The firewall
  If another device cannot connect, this computer's firewall may need a rule that allows the App's
  port from your network.


